The site does not adapt to system-wide dark mode settings, which are recommended in Apple's HIG for better readability in low-light environments.

## Why is this an issue?

- Users who prefer dark mode (for accessibility or comfort) do not get an optimized experience.
- Apple’s HIG suggests respecting system-wide settings for seamless user experience.

### Suggested Fix:

Implement a CSS media query to detect prefers-color-scheme: dark.

See this amazing article :)

[https://www.esri.com/about/newsroom/arcuser/mobile-media-friendly/
](https://www.esri.com/about/newsroom/arcuser/mobile-media-friendly/
)
```
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body {
    background-color: #121212;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
}
```

