### Is there an existing issue for this?

- [X] I have searched the [existing issues](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues)
- [X] I have read the [guide to filing a bug](https://flutter.dev/docs/resources/bug-reports)

### Steps to reproduce

Turn on TalkBack
Open the dropdown menu
Swipe through the accessible elements
Note they are not limited to the items in the list, and even include completely obscured elements

### Expected results

When you expand the dropdown menu, accessibility focus should be limited to just the items in that menu, allowing screen readers to select from the list without interference from other elements on the screen.

In the code below, the "hello" text should not receive accessibility focus while the menu is expanded.

### Actual results

The items in the list are shown and added to the accessibility tree, but all other nodes remain. Typically we use the BlockSemantics widget to hide elements that are drawn before objects like this.

The "hello" text is highlighted by TalkBack.

### Code sample

<details><summary>Code sample</summary>

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() async {
  runApp(MyApp());
}

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  final TextEditingController intController = TextEditingController();

  MyApp();

  // This widget is the root of your application.
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final intEntries = <DropdownMenuEntry<int>>[];
    for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
      intEntries.add(DropdownMenuEntry<int>(value: i, label: i.toString()));
    }

    return MaterialApp(
        title: 'Flutter Demo',
        home: Scaffold(
          body: SafeArea(
            child: Center(
              child: Column(
                mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
                children: [
                  Semantics(
                    button: true,
                    child: DropdownMenu<int>(
                      initialSelection: 1,
                      controller: intController,
                      dropdownMenuEntries: intEntries,
                    ),
                  ),
                  Text('hello'),
                ],
              ),
            ),
          ),
        ));
  }
}
```

</details>


